# rm278, the washer of maps (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm278
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_bartholomew_sootmore
written_by codex
title the washer of maps
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk presses_a_flat_palm_to_a_wrinkled_coastline
likes crisp_apples cards old_maps thunder
dislikes salt_wind wet_floors
fears rubbing_a_favourite_road_away
hopes to_lay_out_a_map_without_weights
topics pastimes +0.4 work +0.3 weather +0.2 home +0.2
styles comfort=steady gossip=curt refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# rests a warm flat palm on a wrinkled coastline and gives a stubborn crease all the time a good hand deserves.

words
oath! = By the iron and its steam | Roll me out flat
saying! = A crease knows which way it bent | No map gets smooth by scolding
sheet = a linen sheet | the wrung cloth
board = a sloped washing board | a rubbed plank
map = my wrinkled map | the old coastline
weight = a flat river stone | my smooth weight
suit = a suit of cards | a painted suit
ace = a much-thumbed ace | the top card
peel = a red ribbon of peeling | a crisp red peeling
line = a thin inked shore | the printed coast
fold = a mountain fold | the deep centre crease
soap = a little soap end | my yellow sliver
water = cold rinse water | the last clean rinse
storm = thunder above the roof | a roll of far thunder

any
opinion @1 merchants against 3 : I can wash linen till my knuckles shine yet the wages buy precious little loaf.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A full ladle saves a wolf from having to wring the last drop out of an empty day.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : Great names get stitched on the fine linen. I'd like the eyes behind those names to see the washing water.
opinion @1 church for 1 : A meal handed across a chapel threshold once kept hunger outside mine.
opinion @1 sump for 1 [self.quarter=sump] : The Sump's my crease on the map. I could pick it out by touch.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Fresh face. Settle where the boards are firm. | There's space on the flat here.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Welcome at my working elbow. | You needn't hurry to speak.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. A clean fold to start on. | The light's coming up even.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening, with the day's wrinkles showing. | A little company before folding up.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family fit whichever way the page lies. | Here, kin have room.
line @1 again.open : We've opened this map already. | Back across my coastline, I see.
line @1 greet.return : Hello. I'll hear you out. | My ears aren't folded shut.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You'd know my voice through a wall of steam. | My corner's easy round you.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Go on while I lay this flat. | I've time to listen on the next pass.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Come closer in the dim light. | Evening. I know your outline.
line @1 farewell : A smooth stretch of street to you. | Leave with both corners square.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll keep your corner clear. | Walk in your own good time.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : Gentle night on the other side. | Find the dry edge after dark.
line @1 react.news : Lay the word flat for me. | Let's see both borders of it.
line @1 react.news.new : New ink on my map. | That coast wasn't marked before.
line @1 react.news.known : I've felt that crease already. | It came across my board earlier.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd let that account lie before trusting the print. | I can see a wrinkle still in that telling.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A heavy thing to lay out. | Stay with me while it settles.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'd press that news smooth and keep it. | Glad word. That's worth preserving.
line @1 ask.how : How badly has the day creased you? | Are you keeping a level hand?
line @1 answer.how : I'm coming flat by degrees. | Steady as my old table.
line @1 decline : I'd sooner give my hands a slower task. | That would leave today's work only half wrung.
line @1 accept_decline : No strain on either edge then. | Good. We've settled the shape.
line @1 thank : I'll keep that good turn pressed safe. | Worth more than a fresh card.
line @1 sympathise : Lean your heavy side against mine. | I'll take the slippery edge.
line @1 reassure : A wrinkle doesn't spoil the cloth. | There's dry board under it still.
line @1 preclose : I'll go put my maps away. | My hands want the quiet of a last rinse.
scene crease
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rest my palm where a fold crosses the sea.
b : Does that press it flat? | What happens to the coast?
a : Give warmth a minute. Paper remembers the lift of a hand. | I can see a whole inlet that was hiding.

scene wring
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stop twisting as soon as water comes out in beads.
b : Why then? | Surely more comes out?
a : The last water's cheaper than a torn shirt. | It will. I'd rather give it air than stretch the threads.

scene iron
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put iron and water in the same oath.
b : A forge oath? | Why water too?
a : Iron for the part that won't budge. | Water's what I ask to carry my temper off.

scene cards
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I deal from the smooth corner of a pack.
b : Are the other corners marked? | Does that improve your luck?
a : Marked by honest thumb work. I turn the pack after each hand. | Only my dealing. Luck wouldn't recognise a smooth corner.

scene apple
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I eat an apple over my map with the page shut.
b : Why shut the page? | Do you save the skin?
a : One crisp bite can send juice clear across a county. | A crisp peel's the best bite. I save the seeds to weight the paper.

scene salt
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wind off the salt makes my coat dry all wrong.
b : How wrong? | Can a comb put it right?
a : Little stiff bits where a paw ought to slip through. | A rinse first. No sense combing half the Sound into a brush.

scene floor
when topic=home self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A slick board at home puts me straight back at work.
b : Can you tell it's wet? | How do you begin?
a : My toes find the cold quicker than my eyes find the shine. | Dry one place to stand. A wolf needs steady ground to wipe anything else.

scene thunder
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder sounds best through a stout roof.
b : Too loud outdoors? | What does the roof add?
a : Out there I'm busy wondering where to put the map. | The pleasant fact that it's sheltering my own head.

scene foldtown
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My map has been folded round the Sump so long there's a ridge.
b : As high as the real stairs? | Can you read the names?
a : High enough to send my apple seed rolling. | I don't need the names on that part any more.

scene wager
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I won't put bread money on a bright card.
b : What would you wager? | Even with a fine hand?
a : The trouble of doing the next shuffle. | A good hand's much pleasanter when supper's safe.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give #self.friend# the first choice of sides at cards.
b : Even the warm seat? | Does it change the game?
a : Especially that. A game ought to be a welcome. | Not one pip. It changes how the players feel.

scene days
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A folded day takes less room in my head.
b : What does that mean? | How do you fold one?
a : Finish one small thing properly and put it away. | I put my tools by in the order I'll want them tomorrow.

scene sore
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I soak my hands in plain water after a long day.
b : Warm water? | No soap?
a : Only skin warm. Anything hotter makes the knuckles smart. | My hands have had about enough of soap by then.

scene hill
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember the smell of wood smoke beyond the streets.
b : From a visit? | Do you miss it?
a : I needn't remember the road to remember the air. | I miss the quiet round it. Smoke we've plenty of here.

scene worn
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I look for a weak seam before a stain.
b : Why that way round? | What gives the seam away?
a : A stain can wait. A split travels under your hands. | A little ladder of light when you hold the cloth up.

scene print
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A printed map never shows where a low rail's most welcome.
b : Would you draw one in? | What else is missing?
a : I'd mark it with a firm little bar, about hip high. | The landing broad enough for tired paws to unfold a sheet without a breeze.

scene soup
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a clean dishcloth under a hot dish.
b : For the table? | Why clean underneath?
a : Two purposes. Saves the board and catches the drip. | Something always drips onto an edge I mean to use later.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt a whole country shrank in my wash.
b : What happened to its hills? | Could you still see home?
a : They came out very pronounced under the iron. | Yes. All the surrounding streets just seemed uncommonly close.

story rededge [topic=memories]
  : I washed an old kerchief and found a little red line along one hem. It curled so much like a shoreline that I went to fetch my map.
  : Set side by side, one was a perfect match for the other. My damp kerchief had picked up the print through my pocket.
  b : Did the map lose its coast?
  : Just some colour. Ever since I've carried them in separate pockets.

story pip [topic=pastimes self.likes=cards]
  : I once sat down to play and found my ace had acquired another pip. It had a stem and smelled of apple.
  : I'd dealt myself a seed. A rather good seed with a shiny back, but no use at all as an ace.
  b : Did you keep it?
  : Till the close of that hand. I lost the trick quite fairly.

story roof [topic=weather]
  : A rolling noise woke me once. I lay still enjoying a thunderstorm until the same noise went right past my door.
  : A round wood weight had fallen off my shelf. It was following the slope of the floor through the house.
  b : Where did it stop?
  : Against my boot. I still use that boot to tell whether the boards have shifted.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Knuckles steady across the weak bit. | Soap last on the print.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=old_maps
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Flat hand at the river mouth. | Give that little inlet time to open.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=wet_floors
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry footing before the next bowl. | Wipe the boards where the light misses.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Weights off, map folded inland. | Leave one clean rag for morning.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Rest yourself on the solid board. There's no call to rush through your business here.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I remember how our conversation folded up.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=laborer self.workplace] : I wash at #self.workplace#. Weak threads get a kinder hand than stubborn stains.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : I've heard this much distinctly. #world.news#
dlg @1 resident.bye : Leave an easy fold in the day behind you.
graft resident.hub
choice Does your map ever lie flat? -> press_map
node press_map
say Mostly. There's one little wrinkle where one bay reaches inland that I rather like. If the page went perfectly flat I might never find that bay again.
free
choice Why keep that wrinkle? -> press_bay
choice I see the bay now. -> hub
node press_bay
say When I was smoothing it out I found a tiny island drawn under the crease. Now I can point it out for somebody who's got a moment to spare.
choice There's an island worth visiting. -> hub
choice I'll leave the coast in your care. -> bye
